        what: at risk/material_quantitative_output: 'replace-me' is not of type 'boolean'
        fix : Correct the profile. See the worked examples in examples/.
  [SP016] The application profile does not satisfy the control contract
        what: at risk/relied_on_outside_team: 'replace-me' is not of type 'boolean'
        fix : Correct the profile. See the worked examples in examples/.
  [SP024] The profile review date is unreadable
        what: adoption.review_by is 'replace-me', which is not an ISO date.
        fix : Use the YYYY-MM-DD form, for example '2027-02-15'.
  [SP020] The application profile still contains template placeholders
        what: application_id = 'replace-me'; display_name = 'replace-me'; owner = 'replace-me'; risk.relied_on_outside_team = 'replace-me'; risk.material_quantitative_output = 'replace-me'; adoption.framework_version = 'replace-me'; adoption.framework_digest = 'replace-me'; adoption.adoption_date = 'replace-me'; adoption.review_by = 'replace-me'; adoption.framework_maintainer = 'replace-me' (and 9 more)
        fix : Replace every placeholder with a real value. A profile of placeholders records nothing.
  [SP046] secret_hygiene is declared but no scanner is named
        what: baseline_controls.secret_hygiene has no scanner block naming a tool and where it is wired.
        fix : Name the scanner and the file(s) that run it under baseline_controls.secret_hygiene.scanner. This standard requires secret_hygiene at every level; until the scanner is named, the requirement is a declaration with nothing behind it.
  [SP051] Control 'dependency_lock' is required but names nothing to check
        what: control_decisions.dependency_lock has no implementation_reference, so the declaration is compared against nothing.
        fix : Add implementation_reference naming the file that implements this control - a lock file, a findings register. A control checked only against its own declaration is a statement of intent, not a control.
  [SP048] The profile declares a different version from the one installed
        what: adoption.framework_version is replace-me, but .standards/INSTALL.json records 0.17.0 as installed.
        fix : Correct the profile, or re-run the installer. A conformance claim names the version it was assessed against; naming one that is not present makes the claim unverifiable rather than merely wrong.
  [SP049] The profile's framework digest does not match what is installed
        what: adoption.framework_digest is replace-me, but the installed standard anchors to ceffdcf76ae5440ceae16c154893c3771455db0ad7aaa36d245bbe67db4c8d7f.
        fix : Set adoption.framework_digest to the value in .standards/INSTALL.json, or re-run the installer. Note that DR-14 changed this field's meaning: it is now sha256(MANIFEST.sha256), not the release archive's digest, because the archive is not reproducible and so could never be recomputed by anyone checking the claim.
  [SP032] Gate 'work_registration' requires an artefact that does not exist
        what: replace-me is named as a precondition but is not present.
        fix : Create the artefact, correct the path, or change the gate's status. A gate whose precondition cannot be satisfied is not a control.
  [SP033] Gate 'work_registration' has an unreadable effective date
        what: effective_from is 'replace-me', which is not an ISO date.
        fix : Use YYYY-MM-DD, or YYYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss+hh:mm to bind from an instant.
  [SP037] 'builds_user_interface' is not a yes or no
        what: found 'replace-me'.
        fix : Use true or false.

